<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Musi River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Musi River is a river in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> on which the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palembang">Palembang</a> stands. Palembang served as the core capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a>, and its riverine position allowed the state to oversee shipping between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-china-sea">South China Sea</a> through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a> straits.</p></div>
